'''Module:Uptodate helper''' is a helper module for {{t|Uptodate}} that compares revision timestamps across multiple pages and returns data for the most recently edited one.

== Purpose ==

This module eliminates the need for repetitive and expensive parser function calls when comparing revision dates across multiple pages. Instead of calling <code><nowiki>{{REVISIONTIMESTAMP}}</nowiki></code> and <code><nowiki>{{REVISIONUSER}}</nowiki></code> multiple times, the module fetches this data once per page and performs the comparison internally.

== Usage ==

=== Main function ===

Outputs a fully rendered {{t|Uptodate}} template based on the latest revision among the specified pages:

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|main|Page1|Page2|time=18:00|bordercolor=value|utdcolor=value}}
</syntaxhighlight>

=== Individual functions ===

For more granular control, you can use these standalone functions:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Function !! Description !! Example
|-
| <code>page</code> || Returns the page title with the latest revision || <code><nowiki>{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|page|Page1|Page2}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| <code>user</code> || Returns the username of the last editor || <code><nowiki>{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|user|Page1|Page2}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| <code>userlink</code> || Returns a formatted wikilink to the user page || <code><nowiki>{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|userlink|Page1|Page2}}</nowiki></code>
|-
| <code>date</code> || Returns the formatted date via {{t|LastRevision}} || <code><nowiki>{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|date|Page1|Page2}}</nowiki></code>
|}

== Parameters ==

=== Positional parameters ===

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Parameter !! Description
|-
| <code>1</code>, <code>2</code>, <code>3</code>... || Page titles to compare (supports up to 10 pages)
|}

=== Named parameters ===

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Parameter !! Description !! Default
|-
| <code>time</code> || Time value passed to {{t|Uptodate}} || ''none''
|-
| <code>bordercolor</code> || Border color for the Uptodate box || ''template default''
|-
| <code>utdcolor</code> || Text color for the header || ''template default''
|-
| <code>nocat</code> || Disable categorization || ''none''
|-
| <code>discography</code> || Include discography text || ''none''
|-
| <code>needrom</code> || Flag for romanization needed || ''none''
|-
| <code>lastedittext-nolink</code> || Disable link on "last edited" text || ''none''
|}

== Examples ==

=== Basic usage ===

Compare two song list subpages and display the update status:

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{#invoke:Uptodate helper|main
 | Mafumafu/Songs/Cover
 | Mafumafu/Songs/Original
 | time        = 18:00
 | bordercolor = var(--primary-color)
 | utdcolor    = var(--secondary-color)
 | nocat       = true
}}
</syntaxhighlight>

=== Getting just the latest editor ===

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
Last updated by: {{#invoke:Uptodate helper|userlink|Mafumafu/Songs/Cover|Mafumafu/Songs/Original}}
</syntaxhighlight>

=== Manual template call ===

If you need to pass additional parameters to {{t|Uptodate}} that this module doesn't support:

<syntaxhighlight lang="wikitext">
{{Uptodate
 | {{#invoke:Uptodate helper|date|Mafumafu/Songs/Cover|Mafumafu/Songs/Original}}
 |
 | 18:00
 | bordercolor       = var(--primary-color)
 | utdcolor          = var(--secondary-color)
 | customlatesteditor = {{#invoke:Uptodate helper|userlink|Mafumafu/Songs/Cover|Mafumafu/Songs/Original}}
 | nocat             = true
}}
</syntaxhighlight>

== Performance ==

This module significantly reduces parser function calls:

{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Function !! Before (Wikitext) !! After (Lua)
|-
| <code>REVISIONTIMESTAMP</code> || 8 calls || 2 calls
|-
| <code>REVISIONUSER</code> || 4 calls || 1 call
|-
| <code>#time:U</code> || 8 calls || 2 calls
|-
| <code>#ifeq</code> / <code>#ifexpr</code> || 3 calls || 0 calls
|-
! Total !! '''23+ calls''' !! '''5 calls'''
|}

== Error handling ==

The module returns an error message in the following cases:

* No pages specified: <code><nowiki><span class="error">Error: No pages specified for Module:Uptodate helper</span></nowiki></code>
* No valid revision data found: <code><nowiki><span class="error">Error: Could not retrieve revision data for any specified page.</span></nowiki></code>

== Dependencies ==

* {{t|Uptodate}} – The main template this module assists
* {{t|LastRevision}} – Used for date formatting
* [[mw:Extension:Scribunto|Scribunto]] – Required for Lua modules

